When using Spring AI in a restricted enterprise network, I have the same problem:
1. UnknownHostException: Even with http.proxyHost set, the underlying Netty/OkHttp client tries to resolve DNS locally before connecting to the proxy.
2. Proxy Ignored: In dynamic model creation (using OpenAiApi.builder()), the global proxy settings or custom WebClient beans are often ignored.

**The Root Cause**
1. DNS Resolution: Reactive clients (Netty) often use an internal DNS resolver. In internal networks, local DNS can't resolve external domains like openai.com or dashscope.aliyuncs.com.
2. Decoupled Components: Spring AI's OpenAiApi can use either RestClient or WebClient. If you only configure one, the other will fail during specific operations (like streaming or connection testing).

**The Solution**
To solve this, you need to provide a Dual-Client Proxy Configuration to the OpenAiApi.builder(). We recommend using Apache HttpClient 5 for the synchronous RestClient to avoid Spring 6.2 deprecation issues.

Step 1: Add Dependency
Ensure you have the Apache HttpClient 5 in your pom.xml:
```
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.apache.httpcomponents.client5</groupId>
    <artifactId>httpclient5</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

Step 2: Implementation
Use the following pattern in your DynamicModelFactory or Configuration class:

```Java
@Service
public class AiModelFactory {

    @Value("${my.proxy.host}") String proxyHost;
    @Value("${my.proxy.port}") int proxyPort;
    @Value("${my.proxy.username}") String proxyUser;
    @Value("${my.proxy.password}") String proxyPass;

    /**
     * Solution for RestClient (Synchronous) - Fixes Spring 6.2 Deprecation
     */
    private RestClient.Builder getProxiedRestClientBuilder() {
        BasicCredentialsProvider credsProvider = new BasicCredentialsProvider();
        credsProvider.setCredentials(new AuthScope(proxyHost, proxyPort),
                new UsernamePasswordCredentials(proxyUser, proxyPass.toCharArray()));

        CloseableHttpClient httpClient = HttpClients.custom()
                .setProxy(new HttpHost(proxyHost, proxyPort))
                .setDefaultCredentialsProvider(credsProvider)
                .build();

        return RestClient.builder()
                .requestFactory(new HttpComponentsClientHttpRequestFactory(httpClient));
    }

    /**
     * Solution for WebClient (Asynchronous/Streaming) - Fixes UnknownHostException
     */
    private WebClient.Builder getProxiedWebClientBuilder() {
        HttpClient httpClient = HttpClient.create()
                .proxy(p -> p.type(ProxyProvider.Proxy.HTTP)
                        .host(proxyHost)
                        .port(proxyPort)
                        .username(proxyUser)
                        .password(s -> proxyPass));

        return WebClient.builder()
                .clientConnector(new ReactorClientHttpConnector(httpClient));
    }

    public ChatModel createChatModel(ModelConfigDTO config) {
        // Core: Inject BOTH builders into OpenAiApi
        OpenAiApi openAiApi = OpenAiApi.builder()
                .apiKey(config.getApiKey())
