If you are trying to use WebFlux + Spring Security ; the authentication and security context are in the reactor context, but you can't access them from the `@McpTool`-annotated method because it's a blocking method.
Because it's already in the reactor context you don't need a "context extractor", but to get the reactor context you probably have to write your own low-level async tool specs (beware of this code, I haven't tried it):

```java
McpServerFeatures.AsyncToolSpecification.builder()
    .tool(myToolSchema)
    .callHandler((exchange, request) -> {
        return ReactiveSecurityContextHolder.getContext()
                .map(SecurityContext::getAuthentication)
                .map(authentication -> {
                    // do the thing with authentication
                    return "<the result>";
                });
    })
    .build();
```

