# Bug Report: Claude API Connection Prematurely Closed When Processing Images

## Bug description

When using Spring AI's Anthropic Claude API for streaming conversations, pure text conversations work normally, but once an image is uploaded, a connection prematurely closed error occurs (
`Connection prematurely closed BEFORE response`). The OpenAI API works normally in the same scenario, and the issue only appears with the Claude API.

<img width="814" height="251" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc19a068-5912-4687-873f-0577246b1c30" />

<img width="815" height="363" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a173ab82-1e64-4367-86c0-ed8e07fd41a4" />

<img width="808" height="367" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3798369-b278-4504-932b-a54995a45fb9" />

## Environment

- **Spring AI version**: 1.1.0
- **Java version**: jdk17
- **Spring Boot version**: 3.3.13
- **Vector Store**: Qdrant
- **Dependencies**:
    - `spring-ai-starter-model-anthropic`
    - `spring-ai-starter-model-openai`
    - `reactor-netty-http`
    - `spring-ai-qdrant-store`

## Steps to reproduce

1. Configure AnthropicApi Bean with custom baseUrl and apiKey
2. Create ChatClient and configure AnthropicChatOptions
3. Use ChatClient for pure text conversation - **Works normally** ✅
4. Upload image file and call `streamChat()` method for streaming conversation
5. System has no response, throws `WebClientRequestException: Connection prematurely closed BEFORE response` after timeout

## Expected behavior

Claude API should be able to handle streaming conversation requests containing images normally like OpenAI API, returning AI responses instead of connection closed errors.

## Actual behavior

- Pure text conversation: Works normally ✅
- Image conversation: Connection prematurely closed, no AI-level error messages ❌
- Direct call to Claude API using the same proxy address (not through Spring AI): Works normally ✅



