    return AnthropicApi.builder()
            .baseUrl(anthropicBaseUrl)
            .apiKey(anthropicApiKey)
            .restClientBuilder(restClientBuilder)
            .webClientBuilder(webClientBuilder)
            .build();
}

@Bean
@RefreshScope
public ChatOptions claudeSonnet_4_5_ChatOptions(@Qualifier("claudeSonnet_4_5") ModelProperties modelProperties) {
    return AnthropicChatOptions.builder()
            .model(modelProperties.getModel())
            .topK(modelProperties.getTopK())
            .topP(modelProperties.getTopP())
            .temperature(modelProperties.getTemperature())
            .build();
}

@Bean
@RefreshScope
public ChatClient claudeSonnet_4_5_ChatClient(
        @Qualifier("anthropicChatModel") ChatModel chatModel,
        MessageChatMemoryAdvisor messageChatMemoryAdvisor,
        ChatOptions claudeSonnet_4_5_ChatOptions) {
    return ChatClient.builder(chatModel)
            .defaultSystem(defaultSystem)
            .defaultAdvisors(messageChatMemoryAdvisor)
            .defaultOptions(claudeSonnet_4_5_ChatOptions)
            .build();
}
```

### Streaming Chat Method (Image Processing Part)

```java
public Flux<String> streamChat(ChatClient chatClient, String query, String conversationId,
                               VectorId vectorId, Rag rag, List<MultipartFile> files) {
    StringBuilder systemPrompt = new StringBuilder();

    // RAG logic omitted...

    List<Media> mediaList = historyMedia.getImages();

    // Process user's currently uploaded files
    StringBuilder fileContentBuilder = new StringBuilder();
    processUploadedFiles(files, mediaList, fileContentBuilder);

    // 3. Build streaming request
    return chatClient.prompt()
            .system(system -> {
                if (!systemPrompt.isEmpty()) system.text(systemPrompt.toString());
            })
            .user(user -> {
                user.text(query);
                if (!mediaList.isEmpty()) user.media(mediaList.toArray(Media[]::new)); // ⚠️ Issue occurs here
            })
            .advisors(a -> a.param(CONVERSATION_ID, conversationId))
            .stream()
            .chatClientResponse()
            .mapNotNull(response -> /* ... */)
            .doOnComplete(() -> {
                mediaStorageService.saveMediaFiles(conversationId, files);
            })
            .onErrorResume(e -> Flux.just(formatErrorMessage(conversationId, e)));
}

private void processUploadedFiles(List<MultipartFile> files, List<Media> mediaList,
                                  StringBuilder fileContentBuilder) {
    if (CollectionUtils.isEmpty(files)) return;

    for (MultipartFile file : files) {
        try {
            String contentType = file.getContentType();
            String fileName = file.getOriginalFilename();

            // Validate file size
            if (!isFileSizeValid(file)) {
                throw new RuntimeException("File exceeds size limit");
            }

            if (contentType != null && contentType.startsWith("image/")) {
                // Image file: as Media object
                MimeType mimeType = MimeTypeUtils.parseMimeType(contentType);
                ByteArrayResource resource = new ByteArrayResource(file.getBytes());
                mediaList.add(Media.builder()
                        .mimeType(mimeType)
                        .data(resource)
                        .build());
                log.debug(imageDebugLog, fileName, file.getSize());
            } else if (isSupportedTextFile(fileName)) {
                // Text file processing
                fileContentBuilder.append(readTextFileContent(file));
            } else {
                throw new RuntimeException("Unsupported file type");
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            log.error("Failed to process file: {}", file.getOriginalFilename(), e);
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to read file: " + file.getOriginalFilename(), e);
        }
    }
}
```

## Additional context

- Direct calls to Claude API using the same proxy address (not through Spring AI) can process images normally

<img width="1047" height="909" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aea0d383-6bb1-4251-93b8-8c1c12433086" />

- OpenAI API processes images completely normally under the same code logic
- Error occurs in `reactor.netty.http.client.HttpClientOperations.onInboundClose`
- No AI-level error messages, only low-level network connection errors
- Suspected to be a request format or timeout configuration issue with Spring AI's AnthropicApi when processing images

## Questions

1. Does Spring AI's AnthropicApi have special restrictions on image size or format?
2. Does WebClient's timeout configuration need special adjustments for image requests?
3. Are additional parameters needed in AnthropicChatOptions to support images?
4. Does streaming response processing require different configuration when handling images?

---

**Note**: This issue only occurs when using Claude API to process images, pure text conversations and OpenAI API both work normally.

