**Bug description**

`OpenAiChatModel.stream(Prompt)` in Spring AI `2.0.0-M5` and `2.0.0-M6` appears to buffer the entire upstream streaming response before emitting any `ChatResponse` downstream.

The method still returns `Flux<ChatResponse>`, but subscribers do not receive chunks as they arrive from the upstream OpenAI-compatible SSE response. Instead, chunks are emitted only after the upstream response has completed.

This happens even when tool calling is not enabled and the response contains no tool calls.

After inspecting the source of `spring-ai-openai`, the issue seems to be caused by `OpenAiChatModel.internalStream(...)` collecting the whole stream before checking whether tool calls exist:
`return flux.collectList().flatMapMany(list -> {
    if (list.isEmpty()) {
