Hello!
I think this ticket explains the situation much better than I ever could: https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-ai/issues/5494

`Developers should be able to designate portions of the system message as static (cacheable) vs dynamic (uncacheable), with buildSystemContent() emitting separate Anthropic ContentBlocks accordingly`

The thing is that the solution that was proposed for the ticket above was implemented for Anthropic and not for Bedrock. When working with Claude models through Bedrock one still runs into the same issue. 

Right now, when working with Bedrock, I can define a list of SystemContentBlocks and set the CachePoint wherever I please. This allows me to have a fixed and cacheable section of the prompt and a portion that will be dynamic and may change either per user or per request:

```
public List<SystemContentBlock> getSystemPromptBlocks(userContext...) {

    return List.of(
            SystemContentBlock.fromText(getFixedSystemPrompt()),
            SystemContentBlock.fromCachePoint(CachePointBlock.builder()
                    .type(CachePointType.DEFAULT)
                    .build()
            ),
            SystemContentBlock.fromText(getDynamicSystemPrompt(userContext...))
    );
  }
```

[This](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-ai/pull/5495) fix was implemented to allow something similar but only for Anthropic.

Could the solution not be made more general in order to support Bedrock too?

