@ThomasVitale ohhh, that makes sense. I will try to reproduce this issue with a larger model a bit later as well (gemma4:26b) cus of memory constraints on my current laptop. 

What I am thinking hypothetically is that ToolCallAdvisor rebuilds instructions from toolExecutionResult.conversationHistory() which includes system, user, assistant tool call and a tool response and then, MessageChatMemoryAdvisor.before() also prepends what it already saved ([user, assistant-toolcall]). So the prompt sent on iteration 2 carries a duplicated user message a duplicated blank assistant-tool-call message. 

