**Bug description**

MCP tool method callback classes from the mcp-annotations package remap exceptions thrown from methods that implement tool calls. Example of one such case with sync stateless callback, similar happens in other cases: [SyncStatelessMcpToolMethodCallback#apply method](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-ai/blob/v2.0.0/mcp/mcp-annotations/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/mcp/annotation/method/tool/SyncStatelessMcpToolMethodCallback.java#L83-L88).

This is OK for most exceptions, but should not be done for instances of `io.modelcontextprotocol.spec.McpError`. These exceptions contain the `jsonRpcError` property which should be returned directly to the MCP client, instead of getting remapped into a `CallToolResult`.

**Environment**

Tested with Spring AI version 2.0.0, with streamable protocol and sync type.
Looking at the code, the same happens in all (streamable / stateless x sync / async) combinations.

**Steps to reproduce**

The exception thrown by this implementation will be remapped into a tool call response, and will not trigger the expected [error flow of the URL mode elicitation](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/client/elicitation#url-mode-with-elicitation-required-error-flow):

```java
package com.example;

import io.modelcontextprotocol.spec.McpError;
import io.modelcontextprotocol.spec.McpSchema;
import org.springframework.ai.mcp.annotation.McpTool;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

import java.util.List;
import java.util.UUID;

@Service
public class ToolService {
    @McpTool
    public String notOk() {
        var urlElicitation = McpSchema.ElicitUrlRequest.builder(
                "Visit the docs first!",
                "https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/index.html",
                UUID.randomUUID().toString()
        ).build();
        throw McpError.URL_ELICITATION_REQUIRED.apply(List.of(urlElicitation));
    }
}
```

**Expected behavior**

This specific exception should not be converted into tool call response and the `jsonRpcError` should be returned to the client.

[Tools registered using the low-level API](https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/api/mcp/mcp-streamable-http-server-boot-starter-docs.html#_tools) work correctly.

For example, this will work as expected:

```java
package com.example;

import io.modelcontextprotocol.server.McpServerFeatures;
import io.modelcontextprotocol.spec.McpError;
import io.modelcontextprotocol.spec.McpSchema;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;

import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.UUID;

@Configuration
class Config {
    @Bean
    public List<McpServerFeatures.SyncToolSpecification> ok() {
        return List.of(McpServerFeatures.SyncToolSpecification
                .builder()
                .tool(McpSchema.Tool.builder(
                                "ok",
                                Map.of(
                                        "type", "object",
                                        "properties", Map.of()
                                )
                        ).build()
                ).callHandler((exchange, req) -> {
                    var urlElicitation = McpSchema.ElicitUrlRequest.builder(
                            "Visit the docs first!",
                            "https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/index.html",
                            UUID.randomUUID().toString()
                    ).build();
                    throw McpError.URL_ELICITATION_REQUIRED.apply(List.of(urlElicitation));
                }).build());
    }
}
```

**Minimal Complete Reproducible example**

See the steps to reproduce and expected behavior sections for code examples. The method annotation example should produce the same result the using the low-level APIs.

