The thing is that the MCP tool call is NOT using the normal jackson2/3 mapping/validation logic via annotations as the http endpoint, but it does its own thing using the com.github.victools:jsonschema dependencies to verify if the incoming mcp tool call has the right schema as far as i know.

------

Context:

In our application we have actually 2 mcp calls: the first one computes the request for the second mcp call. So we would naturally go with code like this:

